~ start
# talk_to entry point for world-Layla (layla_advanced_overlay launches here).
# the chapter 2 intro cutscene does NOT come through here — chapter2_intro.dialogue
# imports this file and jumps straight to post_wake_intro with actors already staged.
if Flags.get_level_flag("layla_post_wake_intro_seen") == true:
	=> companion_hub

# safety net: talked to before the intro somehow ran. stage the pair the way the
# cutscene hand-off would have, then play the intro.
do actor_enter("Fiona", "base", "left")
do actor_enter("Layla", "base", "right")
do actor_flip("Layla", true)
=> post_wake_intro

~ post_wake_intro
# step 2.212: Test Run's "Skip Layla Wake Chat" sets this flag; the wake-up talk is then skipped.
if Flags.get_level_flag("dev_skip_layla_wake_chat") == true:
	do Flags.set_level_flag("layla_post_wake_intro_seen", true)
	=> END
# [post opening cutscene convo with us]
# reached from chapter2_intro.dialogue with Fiona (left) and Layla (right, flipped)
# already on stage over the dimmed live level.
Layla: Fionaaaa! You fell asleep while working again!
# do actor_change("Layla", "angry_1")
Layla: How many times do I need to tell you that you need to rest properly!
Layla: In your own bed! In your own home!
# do actor_change("Layla", "base")
Player: I know, I know.
Player: I just really got into it. Going home would've broken that flow.
Player: Also, what's this thing over me?
Layla: It's my jacket. I kept it over you to keep you warm as you slept.
Player: Oh.
Layla: Wait, lemme take it off you. I'll put it in my car later.
Player: Thanks, Layla.
Player: What time is it? Has the professor come in yet?
Layla: It's 7:30 right now. The professor doesn't come in until 10, usually.
# do actor_change("Layla", "pout")
Layla: And um... Fiona. Would you still help me with what I asked you yesterday?
Layla: You know, the genomic sequencing thing?
Layla: The professor asked me to show him the results first thing after he arrived.
Layla: If I don't do that, I'm doomed!
# do actor_change("Layla", "base")
Player: Sure. I can do that. Shouldn't take me more than ten minutes.
Player: You know that you could easily do it yourself though, right?
Player: Objectively, you're smarter than the average undergrad Research Assistant.
Player: If I can do it in 10 minutes, you should know it's possible for you to do in under an hour.
# layla is shy. TODO: swap for a proper shy expression when the art lands.
# do actor_change("Layla", "pout")
Layla: Umm... I'm glad you think that.
# layla is extra shy
Layla: I would still like to have you do it for me once, if you don't mind...
Layla: I learn faster when you teach me.
Player: No worries. Let's get to the lab ASAP. I need to go home and shower after this.
# do actor_change("Layla", "victory")
Layla: Yaaaaay! Thanks Fiona! I owe you one.
# do actor_change("Layla", "base")
Player: Let's go.
do Flags.set_level_flag("layla_post_wake_intro_seen", true)
=> END

~ companion_hub
# in-world talk_to hub over the dimmed live level. both sprites are staged, mirroring
# the real-world arrangement: layla_character.gd sets layla_player_on_left when the
# interaction fires. facing convention matches the intro: left = unflipped, right = flipped.
if Flags.get_level_flag("layla_player_on_left") == true:
	do actor_enter("Fiona", "base", "left")
	do actor_enter("Layla", "base", "right")
	do actor_flip("Layla", true)
else:
	do actor_enter("Layla", "base", "left")
	do actor_enter("Fiona", "base", "right")
	do actor_flip("Fiona", true)
if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") >= 3:
	Layla is following you with glistening eyes.
	Her scent reminds you of lavender drenched in dew.
elif Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") >= 0:
	Layla follows along, humming to herself.
	Her scent reminds you of lavender drenched in dew.
else
	Layla follows a step behind, quieter than usual.
~ hub_return
# do actor_change("Layla", "base")
What do you want to say to her?

- Ask about our objective [state={{Flags.get_level_flag("lab_keypad_interacted")}}-{{Flags.get_level_flag("jayce_date_hint_given")}}-{{Flags.get_level_flag("julian_password_asked")}}]
	if Flags.get_level_flag("julian_password_asked") == true:
		# step 2.226: Julian's lead. the code is probably one of Greene's DNA dates
		Player: So, the password to the lab might be one of the dates Julian mentioned.
		Player: The date the double helix was discovered...
		Player: Or the day nuclein was discovered. The DNA molecule.
		do actor_effect("Layla", "jump")
		Layla: Yes! That's gotta be it!
		Player: We only need to find a way to... get those dates now.
		Layla: Indeed... with my dead phone and your dumb one, we're not in a great position.
		if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") >= 0:
			do actor_effect("Layla", "tremble")
			Layla: Fiona... what if we can't make it?
			Layla: The professor would never write me a letter of recommendation after that... would he?
			do actor_effect("Layla", "slump")
			Her shoulders slump.
			Player: Don't worry. We've got this.
			Player: We'll figure it out and get in, one way or another.
			Then, as if solely for you, she straightens her back and puts on a brave face.
			do actor_effect("Layla", "nod")
			Layla: Of course! I trust you.
	elif Flags.get_level_flag("jayce_date_hint_given") == true:
		# step 2.222: Jayce couldn't open it, but the password is (probably) a date
		Player: So, it seems like the janitor can't help us much either...
		Player: But... we do know the password's going to be a date.
		Player: Well, most likely.
		if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") < 0:
			Layla: Right. A date.
		else
			do actor_effect("Layla", "jump")
			Layla: Yes! Now we only need to know WHAT date it could be.
		Layla: We should ask someone!
		Player: Probably.
		Player: (But... who?)
	elif Flags.get_level_flag("lab_keypad_interacted") == true:
		# step 2.221: the code didn't work, so the plan is now the janitor
		Player: So, we're locked out of the lab, unfortunately.
		Player: I think we should talk to the janitor there.
		Player: What do you think?
		Layla: Yeah... let's do that.
		do actor_effect("Layla", "tremble")
		Layla: Although, I don't like the way he's been looking at us since we entered the room.
		Player: Yeah, I get it.
		Player: I'll take the lead. And we'll be cautious.
		if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") < 0:
			Layla: Got it.
		else
			do actor_effect("Layla", "nod")
			Layla: Got it!
	else
		Player: So, just to be clear, Layla. All I need to do is go to the lab with you and help with the sequencing, correct?
		Player: Then I can go home and shower, right?
		if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") < 0:
			Layla: Yes. That's all. I won't bother you after that.
		else
			Layla: Yes! That's all I want from you. I promise I won't bug you after that.
		Player: It's alright. You ain't buggin' me.
		Player: Cool. Let's do this, then.
		if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") < 0:
			Layla: Thanks.
		else
			do actor_effect("Layla", "jump")
			Layla: Yay! Thanks, Fiona.
	=> hub_return

- Ask her about the janitor [if Flags.get_level_flag("jayce_introduced") == true]
	do Flags.set_level_flag("layla_talked_about_jayce", true)
	Player: So... that janitor...
	do actor_effect("Layla", "tremble")
	Layla: Yeah, he's so creeepy!
	Layla: We should tread carefully around him, Fiona.
	Player: Oh, don't worry, Layla. I've met thousands like him.
	Player: I'll handle him.
	if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") < 0:
		Layla: ...Whatever you think is best.
	else
		She seems hesitant, but says:
		do actor_effect("Layla", "nod")
		Layla: Okay, sure! If you say so!
	=> hub_return
- Ask her about work [once] [if Flags.get_level_flag("layla_asked_about_work") == false]
	do Flags.set_level_flag("layla_asked_about_work", true)
	Player: You know, I'm happy to help you with this, but I have to ask...
	Player: Why didn't you do it sooner?
	Player: It makes sense to finish off difficult tasks way before deadlines.
	Player: As your mentor, I need to point this out.
	Player: We need to move fast if we want to secure funding.
	do actor_effect("Layla", "slump")
	You notice her shoulders slump after hearing that remark.
	# do actor_change("Layla", "pout")
	Layla: I know... I'm sorry.
	Layla: It's just... I was afraid of messing it up.
	Layla: The equipment is limited, and expensive.
	Layla: If I got it wrong, it would've come out of the lab's pocket.
	Layla: I didn't wanna disappoint the professor.
	if Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") >= 0:
		do actor_effect("Layla", "shy")
		Layla: Or... you.
	do actor_effect("Layla", "turn_away")
	She looks away, but her mind's eye looks toward you.
	What do you wanna say to her?

	- Comfort her [matters]
		do Flags.set_level_flag("layla_work_comforted", true)
		do Flags.add_game_counter("layla_closeness", 1)
		do actor_effect("Layla", "turn_back")
		Player: That's... alright.
		Player: I would only say that you need to believe in yourself more.
		Player: You're better at this than you realize.
		# TODO: shy expression when the art lands.
		do actor_focus("Layla", 1.6, 0.3)
		Layla: ....!
		do actor_effect("Layla", "tremble")
		Her face turns a bright red.
		Layla: Thank you, Fiona.
		Layla: I guess I needed to hear that.
		do actor_unfocus_all(0.4)
		Layla will remember this.
		# do actor_change("Layla", "victory")
		do actor_effect("Layla", "jump")
		Layla: Still, I promise I'll be more punctual!
		Layla: Can't disappoint my prodigious mentor, after all!
		Player: Yeah, yeah.
		Player: Anyway...
		=> hub_return

	- Reprimand her [matters]
		do Flags.set_level_flag("layla_work_reprimanded", true)
		do Flags.add_game_counter("layla_closeness", -1)
		Player: Afraid?
		Player: That sounds like an excuse rather than a reason, to be honest.
		Player: You had days, Layla. Days.
		Player: And if we keep moving at this pace...
		Player: We can say goodbye to funding.
		Unable to meet your gaze, she says:
		do actor_effect("Layla", "tremble")
		Layla: That's not fair, Fiona. I was trying to be careful...
		Player: Careful doesn't get results.
		Player: But unfortunately, results get funding.
		Player: Next time something scares you, come to me sooner.
		Player: Don't... freeze.
		# do actor_change("Layla", "pout")
		do actor_effect("Layla", "slump")
		Layla is looking down. Shuffling her feet.
		Layla: ...Okay.
		do actor_effect("Layla", "turn_back")
		Layla: I'm sorry. I'll do better.
		Player: Good.
		Layla will remember this.
		Player: Anyway...
		=> hub_return

- Ask her about her life [once] [if Flags.get_level_flag("layla_asked_about_life") == false]
	do Flags.set_level_flag("layla_asked_about_life", true)
	Player: So... apart from work, what've you been up to lately?
	if Flags.get_level_flag("layla_work_reprimanded") == true:
		# step 2.234: after a reprimand she's guarded at first, then thaws
		do actor_effect("Layla", "shy")
		Layla: ...
		Layla: You're not about to tell me off again, are you?
		Player: What? No.
		Player: Of course not.
		Layla: Oh?
		Layla: Then... you're asking me about something other than work?
	elif Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") < 0:
		# step 2.236: distant without a reprimand. guarded, but she lets it happen
		do actor_effect("Layla", "shy")
		Layla: ...
		Layla: Why the sudden interest?
		Player: Can't I just ask?
		Layla: I guess you can.
		Layla: Then... you're asking me about something other than work?
	else
		# step 2.216: she can't believe it. a jolt, then a happy, disbelieving double hop.
		do actor_effect("Layla", "shock")
		Layla: Whaaaaaa?
		do actor_effect("Layla", "bounce")
		Layla: You're asking me about something other than work!?
	# worry: she leans in for a proper look.
	do actor_effect("Layla", "lean_in")
	Layla: Are you okay? Do you have a high temperature?
	# she closes the gap herself. Fiona stays put and lets her.
	if Flags.get_level_flag("layla_work_reprimanded") == true or Flags.get_game_counter("layla_closeness") >= 0:
		do actor_approach("Layla", "Fiona", 440.0, 0.5)
		Layla: Come here, lemme touch your forehead.
	Player: I'm okay, actually.
	do actor_effect("Fiona", "nod")
	Player: Guess I just... realized I hadn't asked you that in a minute.
	# it lands. she straightens, notices how close she is, and drifts back, bashful.
	do actor_effect("Layla", "upright")
	do actor_step_back("Layla", 0.8)
	do actor_effect("Layla", "shy")
	Layla will remember that.
	Layla: Oh... okay.
	Layla: Lemme see. Well...
	# do actor_change("Layla", "victory")
	do actor_effect("Layla", "jump")
	Layla: Oh, I watched this movie recently! Devil Wears Grada 2.
	Layla: The first one was my favorite movie of ALL TIME!!!
	# do actor_change("Layla", "base")
	Player: Oh. I see. How'd you like this one then?
	Layla: It was....
	do actor_effect("Layla", "slump")
	Layla: Okay? I guess.
	Layla: I mean, it had its moments, but it lacked something the genius original had, you know?
	Layla: I also feel it had too many product placements?
	# do actor_change("Layla", "pout")
	Layla: Got a bit tiring seeing a cola can company be advertised for the third time...
	# do actor_change("Layla", "victory")
	do actor_effect("Layla", "bounce")
	Layla: But ohmygod. The fashion in it!
	Layla: That remained top notch.
	# do actor_change("Layla", "base")
	Layla: Okay, maybe it was just a lil' bit worse than the last one, if I'm being honest.
	Layla: But that was already such a high bar!
	All of a sudden, she seems more animated.
	Player: I didn't realize you liked fashion that much.
	do actor_effect("Layla", "lean_in")
	Layla: That's because you never asked!
	do actor_effect("Layla", "upright")
	Layla: ... Or maybe I didn't let it show.
	Layla: I dress pretty basic for someone who's into fashion this much.

	- Ask her why she does that [matters]
		do Flags.set_level_flag("layla_life_asked_why", true)
		do Flags.add_game_counter("layla_closeness", 1)
		Player: Oh. Do you mind if I ask why?
		# do actor_change("Layla", "pout")
		# step 2.217: a gentle close-up while she opens up, released before Fiona answers.
		do actor_focus("Layla", 1.35, 0.6)
		Layla: Well, my parents are immigrants...
		Layla: Let's say they raised me in their own way.
		Layla: I was taught not to attract too much attention to myself.
		Layla: Whenever I've tried dressing up, it's led to a lot of mixed feelings, you know?
		do actor_unfocus_all(0.5)
		Player: I see.
		Player: I'm sorry about that. I hope you can find your confidence someday.
		Player: For me, clothes are just a matter of convenience.
		Player: If I could, I'd roam around naked everywhere.
		Player: Unfortunately, that would land me in jail.
		# step 2.212: layla imagines it. she slides left and close so the thought bubble has the right half.
		# TODO: swap to her blushing + thinking expression when the art lands, e.g.
		# do actor_change("Layla", "blush_thinking")
		do actor_focus("Layla", 1.6, 0.45, -1.0, 0.3)
		do hide_dialogue_ui()
		do prop_enter("Thought", "res://conversation/props/layla_thought_bubble.tscn", "right", 330.0, 1.3)
		do prop_call("Thought", "play")
		do show_dialogue_ui()
		Layla: ...
		# the penny drops: she jolts, the screen shakes, and the bubble pops.
		do actor_effect("Layla", "shock")
		do shake(0.35, 9.0)
		do prop_call("Thought", "burst")
		do prop_leave("Thought")
		Player: Layla, you alright?
		Layla: No!
		do actor_effect("Layla", "tremble")
		Layla: I mean - Yes! No no.
		Player: Huh?
		Layla: [speed=0.7]Oh well,[/speed][wait=0.3] [speed=1.5]I think it's getting quite hot in here,[/speed] [wave amp=16 freq=7]hehe?[/wave] [speed=2.6][mutter][small=0.9]What do you think about the weather?[/small] [small=0.84]And what are your thoughts about the[/small] [small=0.78]economic and political state of the world?[/small][/mutter][/speed]
		do actor_unfocus_all(0.4)
		Player: Riiiight.
		Player: Anyway...
		=> hub_return

	- Move on [matters]
		do Flags.set_level_flag("layla_life_moved_on", true)
		Player: I see.
		Player: That's... interesting.
		do actor_effect("Layla", "slump")
		Player: Anyway...
		=> hub_return

- Never mind [Leave]
	=> END
